From 56fd7bf9ebe6051c1a03885ebf3294a3f0f6cbb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OmarAfet <135471287+OmarAfet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:25:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Report the public API hash in the metadata artifact
 notification

A build system can skip compiling a dependent crate again when the public API hash of each of its dependencies did not change. To compare the hashes, it needs to know them without parsing the metadata format, so with `-Zpublic-api-hash` the artifact notification of the metadata file (`--json=artifacts`) now has a `public_hash` field. Cargo can read it like it already reads the notification to start dependents early.

The hash is read from the header of the metadata file through a memory map, which also covers metadata reused from the incremental session directory. The field is left out without the flag, so the notification is unchanged by default.
